<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>How It Works | Chez Session</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css"></head>
<body><header class="site-header"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Behind the counter</p><h1>How this bistro remembers</h1><nav><a href="index.php">Back to the order form</a></nav></div></header>
<main class="container narrow"><section class="panel"><h2>From form to receipt</h2><ol><li><strong>index.php</strong> shows the form and checks the saved session values.</li><li>Submitting the form sends the choices by POST to <strong>process_order.php</strong>.</li><li><strong>order_functions.php</strong> validates each choice, stores it in the session, and prepares the receipt.</li><li>The receipt displays the saved values. If a field was skipped, it displays <strong>(not selected)</strong>.</li><li>Choosing <strong>Order Again!</strong> returns to the same session, so the dropdowns and radio buttons can be restored.</li><li><strong>forget_order.php</strong> clears the session and redirects to a blank form.</li></ol></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Sessions and cookies are different</h2><p>The dessert, drink, and size are stored in <code>$_SESSION</code> on the server. A session ID cookie helps PHP recognize which session belongs to the browser. A separate <code>lastVisit</code> cookie only remembers the time of the previous submitted order; it does not hold the order.</p><p>The browser sends the cookie on later requests. PHP reads the session on the server and prints the matching <code>selected</code> or <code>checked</code> attribute in the HTML.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Why I used fallbacks</h2><p>Someone can submit without making every choice. Rather than causing an undefined-index warning or showing a blank receipt, the code stores <code>(not selected)</code>. The menu values are also checked against the allowed choices, because posted data should not be trusted just because it came from a form.</p></section></main><footer class="container">Thirunavukkarasu Palaniappa · Homework 03</footer></body></html>
